{"agent_id":"ldsw","agent_seq":59,"timestamp":"2026-10-08T18:42:19.834645Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"dd7e3e04-c9da-42cb-9317-22f3d4fb6a30","title":"One image resolver for every container command, and fork-aware image repository","description":"From PR #129 review (#812, ARCH-08/SEC-10). CROSSLINK_CONTAINER_IMAGE is honoured only by container start and container auth; kickoff (clap default), swarm (lifecycle.rs) and sentinel (engine.rs) ignore it, and swarm and sentinel have no override at all. The image repository is hard-coded to ghcr.io/corvidae-coding-projects/crosslink-agent, so a fork's release binaries default to Corvidae's image at the fork's version, while the workflows derive the repository from the owner. Proposal: one resolver (flag, then env, then build default) used at every call site, print where the image came from, and an optional build-time repository override.","priority":"medium","created_by":"ldsw"},"signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAyumIkHlMRsfhsrxO3EPUUzqlrlapOMAn0vCm+jYYqNAl3rF/ko8oC++UsYyQOzdtk577aJGE8FwNeCAuYXgQk="}
